  "note": "The Digimon Pendulum Z's attack table, and ONLY that. It shares the DMX's wire, its five attack types and its level ladder, and it does not share this table: of the sixteen blocks read off a real Pendulum Z, eight also appear in DMX.json and eight appear nowhere in it. The two that do agree at high stages do not even agree about which stage -- PENZ stage 4 lands on DMX stage 4 but PENZ stage 7 on DMX stage 6 -- so these are collisions in a small vocabulary, not a mapping. Never copy a row between the two files. Keyed on the attacker's STAGE and a three-tier band of its LEVEL, then the charge, exactly as DMX.json is; stage 1 has a single band because a Baby I has one level. Read from utilities/DIGIROM/penz.txt and cross-checked against every filmed PENZ battle in utilities/DMX/battle.txt, which reproduces all thirteen. Three middle tiers carry a `provisional` list naming the charges nobody has read; utilities/PENZ/patterns.txt holds the commands that settle them.",
